course: dictionary
lesson: 14529
title: Perpetual: lasting and never stopping
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Perpetual means lasting forever, or happening again and again so often it seems never to stop. Look at the words around it for clues. «My brother's perpetual whining made me cover my ears.» The whining goes on and on, so perpetual tells you it never seems to end.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. «My brother's never-ending whining made me cover my ears.» It still makes sense, so you have the right meaning.
explain: Perpetual is a formal word, so you will often meet it in books, science and maths. Its clues are usually words like forever, always, again and again, or never stopping.
fact: Perpetual means lasting forever or for a very long time.
fact: Perpetual can also mean happening again and again, so often it seems never to stop.
fact: «Perpetual motion» means movement that would go on forever without any energy.
fact: A perpetual motion machine is impossible, because energy is always lost.
fact: Perpetual is an adjective, so it describes a noun, as in «perpetual snow» or «perpetual complaints».
exercise: «The top of the mountain has perpetual snow.» What does perpetual mean here? | *Lasting forever, never melting away | Hidden by clouds | Cold for one day only | Covered in green grass
exercise: «Ben made perpetual complaints about his bedtime.» What does perpetual suggest? | Ending quickly | Sleeping very well | *Complaining again and again, so it seems never to stop | Complaining once, very quietly
exercise: Why is a perpetual motion machine impossible? | It needs paint | It is too big to build | *It would need energy that is always lost | It runs on batteries
test: «The wall clock has a perpetual calendar that never needs changing.» What does perpetual mean here? | *Working year after year without needing changing | Loud and ticking | Broken and stopped | Made of paper
test: «The tiles made a perpetual pattern that went on forever.» What does perpetual mean in this sentence? | A pattern with only three tiles | A pattern made in one minute | A pattern drawn in pencil | *A pattern that goes on without end
exam: Which word could replace perpetual in «The perpetual snow never melted»? | *everlasting | tiny | sudden | brief
